Part 4 opens within the discussion of humanity imagining Poseidon, continued from `maji_kadavulgal3.md`. It ends mid-sentence after `தன்`, completed by `வேலைக்குச் சென்று விட்டான்` in `maji_kadavulgal5.md`; the English ending reflects that boundary.

Conventional English names are used for source forms including `பாசிடன்` (Poseidon), `டைடான் ஓஷியானஸ்` (Titan Oceanus), `லயாமிடான்` (Laomedon), `ஹெஸியோன்` (Hesione), `ஹெர்குலிஸ்` (Hercules), `ஆம்பிடிரைட்` (Amphitrite), `டிரிடன்` (Triton), `இடாஸ்` (Idas), `மார்ப்பேசா` (Marpessa), `ஈவினஸ்` (Evenus), `அபாலோ` (Apollo), `லாடோனா` (Latona), `டீலாஸ்` (Delos), `கிளைமின்` (Clymene), `க்யூபிட்` (Cupid), `டாப்பீன்` (Daphne), and `ப்யேடன்` (Phaethon). Tamil OCR is retained verbatim.

The source appears to call Pluto the wielder of the thunderbolt in the physician-son episode and does not name that son. The translation preserves the source’s presentation rather than silently replacing it with a harmonized classical account.

Several isolated OCR debris strings and damaged line fragments are retained only in the source block.
